P(3 girls∣n=3)=
C(3, 3)*(0.5) ^3* (0.5) ^0
 =1×0.125=0.125
Expected number of girls with sisters (2 girls or 2+ girls) from these families: 
k×P(k∣n)×P(n)=2×0.375×0.15 + 3×0.125×0.15  = 0.16875

For families with 4 children (n=4, P(3)=0.1):
A girl has a sister if there are 2 girls in the family (k=2)
Probability of 2 girls in a family of 4: 
P(2 girls∣n=4)=
