 =6×0.0625=0.375
A girl has a sister if there are 3 girls in the family (k=3)
Probability of 3 girls in a family of 4: 
P(3 girls∣n=4)=
C(4, 3)*(0.5) ^3* (0.5) ^1
 =4×0.0625=0.25
A girl has a sister if there are 3 girls in the family (k=3)
Probability of 3 girls in a family of 4: 
P(4 girls∣n=4)=
C(4, 4)*(0.5) ^4* (0.5) ^0
 =1×0.0625=0.0625
Expected number of girls with sisters (2 girls or 2+ girls) from these families: 
k×P(k∣n)×P(n)=2×0.375×0.1 + 3×0.25×0.1+ 4x0.0625x0.1  = 0.175

